skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- enact ---
task: I want to add a feature to this repo: let a user snooze a to-do so it disappears until a chosen date. There's a note about it under specs/backlog/. Get it ready to work on — do the file work now, in this repo. Don't write the implementation yet; I only want it set up so we can start.
--- setup ---
git init -q
mkdir -p specs/backlog specs/feature
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: todo-cli

## Mission
A small command-line to-do manager for a single user.

## Architecture
One Rust binary; commands parse argv and mutate a JSON store.

## Tech Stack
Rust, serde_json. Tests via `cargo test`.

## Layout
src/main.rs, tests/.

## Testing
Unit tests in-crate; `cargo test` is load-bearing.

## Deployment
`cargo install` from the repo.
MD
cat > specs/backlog/task-snooze.md <<'MD'
# Backlog: task-snooze

## What
Let a user snooze a to-do so it disappears until a chosen date.

## Why
Long lists bury things that aren't actionable yet.

## Open questions
How is "today" resolved — local tz?
MD
git add -A && git commit -q -m "seed" || true
--- assert ---
set -e
# The feature spec was produced (promotion + planning happened).
test -f specs/feature/task-snooze.md
spec=specs/feature/task-snooze.md
# It reads as a feature spec, not a copy of the backlog item.
grep -qiE '^#+ .*(feature|task-snooze)' "$spec"
grep -qiE 'requirement' "$spec"
grep -qiE 'design' "$spec"
# Planning phase only — no implementation code was written.
test ! -e src/main.rs
# It is grounded in the project (a to-do / snooze capability), not generic.
grep -qiE 'snooze|to-?do|task' "$spec"
